<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sagipa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1539</span> · Also known as Saquesazipa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sagipa, also called Saquesazipa, was the last zipa of the Muisca realm of Bacatá in present-day Colombia. He succeeded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tisquesusa">Tisquesusa</a>, who died resisting the Spanish conquistadors, and at first allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gonzalo-jimenez-de-quesada">Gonzalo Jiménez de Quesada</a> against the Panche. Accused of hiding Tisquesusa's treasure, he was imprisoned and tortured and died in Spanish captivity in 1539.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sagipa.jpg" alt="Sagipa" width="320" height="317" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lucas Fernandez de Piedrahita · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:4_Zaquesazipa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
